/ds000001\u003e\n\n```\n```","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475499656,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgxMDIyODg1OA=="},"added":["WIP"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475499948,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTEwMDU5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/875#issuecomment-251100591"},"message":"On Mon, 03 Oct 2016, Michael Hanke wrote:\n\n\u003e    FTR: Starting point in #959 is:\n\u003e \n\u003e    ````mih@meiner /tmp % datalad install ///openfmri/ds000001\n\u003e    2016-10-03 13:36:35,180 [INFO ] Installing dataset at: /tmp/ds000001\n\u003e    (install.py:461)\n\u003e    2016-10-03 13:36:47,675 [INFO ] Initializing annex repo at /tmp/ds000001\n\u003e    (install.py:484)\n\u003e    1 installed item is available at\n\u003e \n\u003e    mih@meiner /tmp % datalad install ///openfmri/ds000001\n\u003e    2016-10-03 13:36:50,550 [INFO ] Installing dataset at: /tmp/ds000001\n\u003e    (install.py:461)\n\u003e    2016-10-03 13:36:50,638 [INFO ] appears to be installed already.\n\u003e    (install.py:176)\n\u003e    2016-10-03 13:36:50,651 [INFO ] Initializing annex repo at /tmp/ds000001\n\u003e    (install.py:484)\n\u003e    1 installed item is available at\n\nThis \"initializing annex repo\" is confusing to say the least since it\nmust not reinitialize annex in the installed dataset.  I would vote to\nremove that log line from within 'get' (or lower to DEBUG and also\nchange msg to \"Passing to AnnexRepo.**init** for possible\n(re-)initialization\" ) and raise log lines in AnnexRepo.**init**\n(there is one for initialization with exactly the same message but\ntrailing ...) to the INFO level.  Then it would be clear when things are\nactually initialized or not.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475501223,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTEwNTA4MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/875#issuecomment-251105081"},"message":"Reinstall now looks like\n\n```\n% datalad install ///openfmri/ds000001\n2016-10-03 15:26:10,247 [INFO   ] \u003cDataset path=/tmp/ds000001\u003e was already installed from http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000001/.git. Use `update` to obtain latest updates (install.py:442)\n1 installed item is available at\n\u003cDataset path=/tmp/ds000001\u003e\n```","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475516728,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgxMDYzNjgwMA=="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475516728,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50ODEwNjM2ODAx"},"added":[],"removed":["WIP"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1484815160,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3MzcxMjg2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/875#issuecomment-273712860"},"message":"@yarikoptic Please say if this can be closed. And if not, what needs to be done.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1485186147,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NDUyMjU2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/875#issuecomment-274522560"},"message":"to say the truth I am not sure yet how feasible is to have it done without much pain and agreeing on desired action(s) to happen.\n\n- Ideally, I see it not exiting early if target is installed already but just possibly skipping some steps if they are already satisfied.  For instance, if I first did `datalad install openfmri`, which installed just top level `openfmri` sub-super-dataset and then call `datalad install -r openfmri` -- it should go and make sure that it recursively got all subdatasets installed as well.  If then I call it again adding `-g` -- it would also fetch all the data.\n\n- related question would be -- should we update/upgrade (\"git pull --ff-only\" kinda)? e.g. compare with `pip install` -- that one would not \"install\" a module again if it was installed already (of some version) but would upgrade it to the latest if we say `--upgrade`.  Or in other words -- if I ran `install openfmri` a week ago, its state (on its origin) if I did it now could be different, so if I just skip updating, overall premise for up-to-date openfmri would not be satisfied.  Having explicit `--update` could make it obvious somewhat.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1489597188,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTAwMTI3NTg2MA=="},"added":[],"removed":["fix-implemented"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493050601,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5NjcyNTA0NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/875#issuecomment-296725045"},"message":"FTR: this is the situation on #1468 \n\n````\nmih@meiner /tmp % datalad --output-format json install ///openfmri/ds000001\n[INFO   ] Cloning dataset from 'http://datasets.datalad.org/openfmri/ds000001' to '/tmp/ds000001' \n{\"action\": \"clone\", \"path\": \"/tmp/ds000001\", \"source_url\": \"///openfmri/ds000001\", \"status\": \"ok\", \"type\": \"dataset\"}\nmih@meiner /tmp % datalad --output-format json install ///openfmri/ds000001\n{\"action\": \"clone\", \"path\": \"/tmp/ds000001\", \"source_url\": \"///openfmri/ds000001\", \"status\": \"notneeded\", \"type\": \"dataset\"}\n````\n\nBoth commands return with zero exit code. `--on-failure` is available as an option to select the desired error behavior.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1493051010,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5NjcyODE4NQ==","github-url